Creating your own unit testing

UNIT TESTS SHOULD NOT BE PRESENT IN THE MAIN BRANCH, in your own branch they can stay (for progress)
Make your own directory for unit testing, the best place is probably within include_emulate/ (as in dont go too far down from here)
Then just follow the similar format in Makefile as the example test for test_register GUIDE BELOW
Example (if you read the Makefile you will see this)

TEST_REGISTER_OBJS = include_emulate/memory_registers_tests/test_registers.o \
        include_emulate/registers/registers.o

test_registers: $(TEST_REGISTER_OBJS)
        $(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o test_registers $(TEST_REGISTER_OBJS)


So when you run this on command line you run
make test_registers
./test_registers
(OUTPUT WILL SHOW)


GUIDE
-------------------------------
So basically in the example above the OBJS will involve the object files of the paths of 1. the test file and 2.the files that you #include in your testing file (thats wordy but should make sense)
MAKE SURE to separate with a backslash before adding more then write the rest of your #include paths (so each path is separated with \)
Then replace anywhere with test_registers which your test file name (the .c file) and just copy everything else like this

X_OBJS = test_path.o \
	include1.o \
	include2.o ...

x: $(X_OBJS)
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o x $(X_OBJS)


